                      "text": "`tests/test_invoice_tax.py` failed with `AssertionError: assert Decimal('10.00') == Decimal('10.01')` because `src/invoice_tax.py` uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). Should I switch it to `ROUND_HALF_UP` for commercial invoicing, or update the test expectation?"
